My core contribution this year was taking ownership of critical CubIQ components and delivering services that improved how Market Risk calculates, validates, and accesses data.

**MRV Builder and CubIQ validation.** I designed and implemented MRV Builder, which generates calculations in the CubIQ Power BI semantic model from user-provided definitions. I extended its APIs to manage calculations and metadata and enable integration with the Marvel UI. MRV Builder covered 100% of existing on-premises MRVs, extended the range of supported calculations, and achieved over 98% accuracy in results. I also built a Spark-based reconciliation framework in Databricks to compare approximately 2,500 MRV calculations against the on-premises baseline. Daily reconciliation helped the team identify data and calculation discrepancies earlier and verify fixes against the agreed acceptance criteria.

**OneRisk data delivery.** I partnered with OneRisk to resolve a performance bottleneck in its data-loading pipelines. I designed and implemented a service that retrieves MRV results directly from CubIQ Delta tables using Databricks Metric Views. This enabled OneRisk to complete its loads within the agreed SLA and reduced demand on the shared Power BI semantic model.

**Marvel Self-Service and report traceability.** I developed an API that versions user changes to Power BI reports in Azure Data Lake Storage (ADLS). This gives Marvel Self-Service a version history so changes to reports can be tracked over time.

**Marvel Explorer and Hybrid replacement.** I designed an API that connects directly to AGrid to retrieve DS2 data and implemented the underlying remote procedure call (RPC) component using the Internet Communications Engine (ICE). This enables Marvel Explorer to process DS2 requests and supports the broader effort to replace the Hybrid application.

**Engineering quality and release ownership.** I built the base CubIQ Power BI semantic model in TMDL and established a CI/CD process aligned with UBS release practices. I implemented unit tests that achieved over 80% code coverage on both MRV Builder and the CubIQ semantic model. I also led the upgrade of our .NET components from .NET 8 to .NET 10.
